For high availability, we aim to achieve the required 99.9% uptime by designing a highly available architecture that takes advantage of cloud providers' built-in redundancy and failover capabilities. Our experience with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, Outscale (SecNumCloud), and Azure (EU regions) allows us to deploy the solution on an infrastructure that meets the EU hosting requirement.

To integrate with the existing system of information, business softwares, electronic management of documents, and user directories, we will employ API standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP (legacy), utilizing API gateways like Kong, Apigee, or AWS API Gateway. Our experience with message brokers including Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ also facilitates integration with various systems.

For data protection and GDPR compliance, we will implement security design patterns such as Zero-trust network architecture, VLAN segmentation, mTLS between services, AES-256 encryption at rest, and TLS 1.3 in transit. Additionally, we will use secrets management tools like HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur to securely manage sensitive data.

To meet the hosting requirement within the European Union, we can deploy the solution on a SecNumCloud-type infrastructure, such as Outscale, which ensures sovereignty over the data and compliance with EU regulations. 

Finally, our experience with monitoring tools including Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack enables us to set up comprehensive monitoring and logging for the solution, ensuring prompt detection and resolution of any issues that may arise.

By leveraging these technologies and our expertise, we can design a robust, scalable, and secure architecture that meets the client's technical requirements while ensuring strict GDPR compliance and high availability.
